The step now prints the directory and says to use the printed path,
because the Bash tool in Claude Code starts a fresh shell for each
command, so `d` from one command is gone in the next. The Edit tool
also needs an absolute path, which the printed one is.

Assumed, not sourced: whether Claude Code asks for permission before
the Edit or Write tool writes under .git/. peff-commit already has the
model write its draft and brief under the git dir, so this is not a
new kind of write, but I did not check how the permission modes treat
it.

The file names inside the directory drop the leading `.stage-`
(base-<name> and <name>), since the directory already says what they
are.
